WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.397
Vinnie and Mandy looked in awe at the men.

2
00:00:04.398 --> 00:00:09.325
They were two of the most famous figures in American history.

3
00:00:09.326 --> 00:00:14.769
John Adams would become the second president of the United States.

4
00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:20.944
And Paul Revere would make a famous midnight ride from Boston to Lexington.

5
00:00:20.945 --> 00:00:27.270
He’d ride to warn of the first British attack in the American Revolution.

6
00:00:27.271 --> 00:00:32.884
"I am told you have a message for me," said John Adams to Vinnie.

7
00:00:32.885 --> 00:00:37.547
Vinnie trembled nervously as he gave him the paper.

8
00:00:37.548 --> 00:00:42.583
Both men read the note and spoke in low voices.

9
00:00:42.584 --> 00:00:44.556
"Thank you for delivering this.

10
00:00:44.557 --> 00:00:48.841
John Hancock needs our help," said Paul Revere.

11
00:00:48.842 --> 00:00:51.927
"Can I help?" asked Vinnie.

12
00:00:51.928 --> 00:00:55.403
Adams patted Vinnie on the shoulder.

13
00:00:55.404 --> 00:00:58.871
"You are very brave," he said.

14
00:00:58.872 --> 00:01:04.644
"In a few years, we hope you can enjoy the freedom we are fighting for."

15
00:01:04.645 --> 00:01:08.730
Just then, there was excitement in the street.

16
00:01:08.731 --> 00:01:13.163
Vinnie and Mandy ran to a window and looked out.

17
00:01:13.164 --> 00:01:18.805
A man was calling out in a loud voice as he walked down the street.

18
00:01:18.806 --> 00:01:22.109
Another man was beating a drum.

19
00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:26.705
People were coming out of their houses and following them.

20
00:01:26.706 --> 00:01:30.244
"Who is he?" asked Mandy.

21
00:01:30.245 --> 00:01:34.033
"The town crier," explained Paul Revere.

22
00:01:34.034 --> 00:01:36.824
"He is announcing a town meeting."

23
00:01:36.825 --> 00:01:41.711
"I think we should all attend," said John Adams.

24
00:01:41.712 --> 00:01:45.666
The children followed the men out of the house.

25
00:01:45.667 --> 00:01:48.215
Vinnie turned to Mandy.

26
00:01:48.216 --> 00:01:53.993
"I can’t believe we just met these famous people!" he said.

27
00:01:53.994 --> 00:01:58.746
The townspeople gathered at a church and went inside.

28
00:01:58.747 --> 00:02:04.529
The place filled up quickly as people sat on the long, wooden benches.

29
00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:09.570
John Adams and Paul Revere walked to the front of the church.

30
00:02:09.571 --> 00:02:13.041
Will’s father had just arrived.

31
00:02:13.042 --> 00:02:17.185
Vinnie, Mandy, and Will sat with him.

32
00:02:17.186 --> 00:02:19.909
"Welcome," said Adams.

33
00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:23.144
"We have many things to discuss.

34
00:02:23.145 --> 00:02:27.296
But first, most of you know what happened this morning."

35
00:02:27.297 --> 00:02:32.620
"They had no right to arrest John Hancock!" someone shouted.

36
00:02:32.621 --> 00:02:37.342
"We must do something, now!" yelled another.

37
00:02:37.343 --> 00:02:41.667
Vinnie and Mandy listened and watched closely.

38
00:02:41.668 --> 00:02:46.286
Everyone was allowed to say what he or she felt.

39
00:02:46.287 --> 00:02:52.300
"I say we should just pay the taxes," said one well-dressed man.

40
00:02:52.301 --> 00:02:55.161
Angry voices burst out.

41
00:02:55.162 --> 00:03:00.094
"Are you loyal to the British?" shouted an old man.

42
00:03:00.095 --> 00:03:04.716
"Let’s not question each other’s loyalty," said a young man.

43
00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:07.272
"We are all patriots!"

44
00:03:07.273 --> 00:03:13.406
"Please, please!" cried John Adams, raising both arms.

45
00:03:13.407 --> 00:03:16.009
The room quieted down.

46
00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:20.884
"Americans believe in freedom of speech," he said.

47
00:03:20.885 --> 00:03:24.619
People shouted in agreement.

48
00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:30.866
"But the British have no right to treat us this way!" yelled a man in a red vest.

49
00:03:30.867 --> 00:03:36.055
The room exploded in cheers.

50
00:03:36.056 --> 00:03:38.118
"There will be a war soon,"

51
00:03:38.119 --> 00:03:41.640
said Will’s father, shaking his head.

52
00:03:41.641 --> 00:03:45.093
"Maybe not, Father," said Will.

53
00:03:45.094 --> 00:03:48.939
"The British might allow us to have our freedom."

54
00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:51.407
Vinnie shook his head.

55
00:03:51.408 --> 00:03:53.658
"Your father is right, Will.

56
00:03:53.659 --> 00:03:57.800
There will be a war. Very soon."

57
00:03:57.801 --> 00:04:00.674
Mandy looked all around.

58
00:04:00.675 --> 00:04:04.061
The faces in the room were angry.

59
00:04:04.062 --> 00:04:13.330
Everyone was ready to fight for freedom.

